SUMMARY:Dormition panigiri of Panagia Tourliani\, Ano Mera
LOCATION:Ano Mera\, Mykonos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Panagia Tourliani in Ano Mera's square is the island's spiritual centre\, and on the evening of 14 August\, after the vespers\, the square fills with a free traditional panigiri: local musicians (Lefteris Kantenas in 2026)\, wine\, and dancing until late\, then the liturgy and procession on the 15th. Ano Mera is 15 minutes by bus from Chora and the buses run late that night.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#ano-mera-dormition-panigiri-of-panagia-tourliani-ano-mera
